# Vendored opus_dnn (RADE/FreeDV voice codec dependency) - committed subset.
#
# We deliberately commit ONLY what the MSBuild-only CI build needs to link
# ChannelMaster:
#   - prebuilt/         the opus.lib binaries (Release+Debug), built once via CMake
#   - include/ dnn/ celt/ silk/  the DSP headers the host/CI compilation references
#   - commit_pin.txt    provenance + the exact CMake rebuild recipe
#
# We do NOT commit the opus / RADE SOURCE (celt/*.c, dnn/*.c, silk/*.c, torch
# training scripts, docs, build config ...). The prebuilt .lib already contains
# that compiled code; if a rare source rebuild is ever needed we re-download the
# pinned commit from upstream + the RADE weight tables (see commit_pin.txt), then
# regenerate prebuilt/ via CMake. Keeping source out of git keeps this vendored
# dir small and matches the locked "vendor the built lib, don't build in CI"
# decision (see FREEDV_HANDOFF.md A6 / B6).

# --- Prebuilt opus.lib (vendored binary, linked by ChannelMaster / CI) ---
!prebuilt/
!prebuilt/**/
!prebuilt/**/*.lib
!prebuilt/**/*.pdb

# --- SIMD headers under x86/ arm/ (repo-root .gitignore global x86/arm rules
#     would otherwise drop these DSP headers we DO commit) ---
!celt/x86/
!celt/x86/**/
!celt/arm/
!celt/arm/**/
!dnn/x86/
!dnn/x86/**/
!dnn/arm/
!dnn/arm/**/
!silk/x86/
!silk/x86/**/
!silk/arm/
!silk/arm/**/
!silk/fixed/x86/
!silk/fixed/x86/**/
!silk/fixed/arm/
!silk/fixed/arm/**/
!silk/float/x86/
!silk/float/x86/**/

# --- CMake scratch output (never commit generated build dir) ---
build/

# --- Anything not explicitly re-included above stays ignored (source, docs) ---
*.c
dnn/torch/
dnn/training_tf2/
tests/
src/
celt/dump_modes/
